\f3\b \cf0   Proposed ADR backlog (ADR-1 through ADR-9)         
\f1\b0                                                                                                                                                                \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \
  Using the Y-Statement shape from your Research folder \'97 one line each, expand the ones you want to commit to first.                                                                                               \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \
  ADR-1: Bounded contexts via DDD                                                                                                                                                                                   \
  In the context of three distinct problem domains (Ticketing & Passes, Visitor Activity Tracking, Asset Telemetry), we faced the challenge of avoiding a single monolithic "estate system," decided on separate    \
  bounded contexts with explicit context maps, and neglected a shared unified data model, to achieve independent evolution and team/AI-assisted ownership per domain, accepting integration overhead between       contexts.                                                                                                                                                                                                         \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \
  ADR-2: Edge-to-cloud connectivity strategy    In the context of patchy park WiFi and budgeted MQTT-capable devices, we faced the challenge of getting telemetry reliably off-site, decided on MQTT with local brokers/store-and-forward gateways, and neglected   direct device-to-cloud HTTP, to achieve resilience to connectivity gaps, accepting eventual-consistency and buffering complexity at the edge.                                                                     \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \
  ADR-3: Telemetry ingestion & streaming backbone                                                                                                                                                                   \
  In the context of continuous ride/animal sensor streams plus visitor-count spikes at open/close, we faced the challenge of choosing an ingestion platform, decided on a managed event-streaming/IoT-hub service     (e.g., cloud IoT Core + Kafka-compatible stream) feeding downstream consumers, and neglected batch-only ETL, to achieve near-real-time popularity and health insights, accepting the operational cost of a          streaming platform.                                                                                                                                                                                               \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \
  ADR-4: Time-series & telemetry storage                                                                                                                                                                            \
  In the context of high-volume rides/animal-enclosure sensor data, we faced the challenge of picking a store, decided on a time-series database (e.g., TimescaleDB/InfluxDB-class) separate from transactional        data, and neglected forcing telemetry into the same relational store as ticketing, to achieve efficient range queries and retention/rollup policies, accepting an additional data store to operate.               \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \
  ADR-5: Ticketing & passes system                                                                                                                                                                                  \
  In the context of needing ticket/family-pass sales that must scale 10x, we faced the challenge of build-vs-buy, decided on [build-a-thin-domain-service in front of a proven payments provider \'97 to be confirmed],  and neglected a full bespoke payments stack, to achieve faster delivery and PCI-scope reduction, accepting vendor coupling for payments.                                                                          \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \
  ADR-6: Safety-critical isolation for ride telemetry                                                                                                                                                               \
  In the context of ride telemetry sharing infrastructure with general analytics, we faced the challenge of keeping safety-relevant signals (ride faults, e-stops) trustworthy, decided on isolating safety-critical\
  alerting on a separate, higher-priority path from analytics telemetry, and neglected routing everything through one general-purpose pipeline, to achieve fast, dependable fault response, accepting duplicated      plumbing for two paths.                                                                                                                                                                                           \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \
  ADR-7: Elasticity & capacity strategy                                                                                                                                                                             \
  In the context of 5,000
\f4 \uc0\u8594 
\f1 15,000 daily visitors and open/close traffic spikes, we faced the challenge of sizing infrastructure, decided on autoscaling cloud-native compute sized for 10x current peak, and         \
  neglected fixed-capacity on-prem servers, to achieve headroom for growth and new future projects, accepting variable cloud cost.                                                                                  \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \
  ADR-8: Visitor data privacy & consent                                                                                                                                                                             \
  In the context of tracking visitor movement/activity for popularity insights, we faced the challenge of balancing analytics value with privacy law, decided on anonymized/aggregated visitor-flow analytics with   opt-in for anything personally identifying, and neglected raw individual tracking by default, to achieve regulatory compliance and visitor trust, accepting reduced granularity in some analyses.                 \
                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \
  ADR-9: AI integration points                                                                                                                                                                                      \
  In the context of the explicit brief to foreground AI value, we faced the challenge of where to apply it rather than bolting it on everywhere, decided on three targeted uses \'97 anomaly detection on              \
  animal-health/ride telemetry, demand prediction for staffing/popularity, and a visitor-facing recommendation/concierge assistant \'97 and neglected a single "AI does everything" approach, to achieve measurable    \
  business value tied to the stated challenges, accepting the need for model governance and monitoring per use case.                                                                                                \
